      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}+2}{{x}^{3}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{{y}^{2}+2}{{x}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-({y}^{2}+2)\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3({y}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
